WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.560
- Yellowstone was so huge.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.550
It's such a huge show, right?

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.980
Like, how, were you,
were y'all both nervous

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.480
about stepping into the prequel thing

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.010
or were you excited because there were,

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.900
there's already this huge fan base?

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.777
- Gosh, you don't want to go do something

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:13.590
that they're not gonna like, you know.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.990
You have so much respect
for Kevin and the cast

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.700
and certainly Taylor,
who wrote 1883 as well.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.250
I mean, you, you wanna,
you wanna, you know,

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.140
live up to the, to the expectations

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.090
of what everybody expects
out of Yellowstone.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.130
You want 'em to expect
the same thing from 1883,

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.030
you wanna live up to it.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.160
- And you certainly want
the cast to like it,

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.050
but at the end of the day, you,

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.840
you trust the writing,
you trust the directing,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.867
and then you trust your fellow actors

00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:41.088
to show up every day on set and deliver.

00:00:41.088 --> 00:00:44.190
And I'm telling you,
every actor on this show

00:00:44.190 --> 00:00:46.530
and every, and I wanna shout
out to the crew members,

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:48.480
the wranglers, and the stunt guys.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.240
Everybody brought their
A-game every single day.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.100
And these were really tough conditions.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.327
It was a really tough shoot

00:00:54.327 --> 00:00:56.070
and everybody just flat brought it.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.110
And I couldn't imagine working

00:00:58.110 --> 00:00:59.460
with a better group of people.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:02.520
- I well, and I honestly,
it was a brilliant play.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.370
Like, what a smart, you know,
play to do a prequel to that.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:07.140
Like, I was one of those
people that love Yellowstone.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.510
So, 1883 was such a, a brilliant play.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:11.670
So, I gotta say, you said conditions.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.830
So, I know that y'all filmed
a bit in Texas where I'm from.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.420
Actually, I'm from Fort Worth where y'all,

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.860
y'all shot at like the stock yards, right?

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.693
- Yeah, oh yeah.

00:01:17.693 --> 00:01:20.394
- That was the first place I
ever snuck into a club, hey!

00:01:20.394 --> 00:01:22.320
- Woo.
(laughing)

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.420
- Only did it once, Mom.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:26.910
But anyway, it was, it
had to be hot, right?

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.490
Where y'all are shooting, and
y'all are layered up, right?

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:31.590
- Oh, a corset and
everything. I felt, yeah.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.390
Sweat poured down parts of my body

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.950
I didn't know sweat could
pour down. It was...

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:36.120
- [Kelly] Oh.
- Really. It was rather.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.107
- You haven't gotten
into spanks yet, yeah.

00:01:37.107 --> 00:01:39.420
- No, no, I'm not there yet.
(laughing)

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:41.250
Yeah, I'm waiting for that one to come.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:45.690
But yeah, but you know, I kind
of also enjoyed it somewhat

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:46.860
because I feel like-
- [Kelly] I like the heat.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.650
- Well that, but you also,
you kind of wanna be miserable

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.420
because that's exactly what,

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.253
- [Kelly] They would've been doing.

00:01:52.253 --> 00:01:54.360
- Yeah. Those conditions
were, it was so authentic.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.260
It was so real.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.710
It was so visceral that
I don't think many of us,

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:01.434
when it came to weather
conditions were acting.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:02.400
(laughing)
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.490
- 'Cause we were genuinely
sweating our, our BA.

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:07.980
- [Kelly] Behinds off. No, you
kept it talk-show friendly.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.270
That was nice, yeah.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.633
Way to go you classy
individual. (laughing)

